{
  "action": "After a standard system update you need to reboot your computer to make all\nthe necessary changes.",
  "description": "It was discovered that OpenSSL incorrectly allocated memory buffers in the\nSSL/TLS state machine when receiving handshake data. A remote attacker\ncould possibly use this issue to cause OpenSSL to consume excessive memory,\nleading to a denial of service. This issue is known as the \"HollowByte\"\ndenial of service.",
